{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "title": "Lesson 2: Ball drop",
  "description": "A ball falling towards the ground: speed, kinetic energy and potential energy as it falls. Built from Ver2_Images_for_inquiry.pptx slides 26-32. Media values marked REPLACE_ME are placeholders.",
  "variables": [
    { "key": "ballMass", "label": "Ball mass", "unit": "kg", "role": "input", "min": 1, "max": 50, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
    { "key": "dropHeight", "label": "Drop height", "unit": "m", "role": "input", "min": 1, "max": 100, "step": 1, "default": 20 },
    { "key": "speed", "label": "Ball speed/velocity", "unit": "m/s", "role": "output" },
    { "key": "kineticEnergy", "label": "Kinetic energy", "unit": "J", "role": "output" },
    { "key": "potentialEnergy", "label": "Potential energy", "unit": "J", "role": "output" },
    { "key": "elapsedTime", "label": "Time", "unit": "s", "role": "output" }
  ],
  "simulation": {
    "key": "ballDrop",
    "adapter": "netsblox",
    "source": "https://physics.c2stem.org",
    "owner": "NaveedMohd",
    "project": "ssmv_26_inquiry2",
    "inputs": {
      "ballMass": "ball mass",
      "dropHeight": "drop height"
    },
    "outputs": {
      "speed": "speed",
      "kineticEnergy": "kinetic energy",
      "potentialEnergy": "potential energy",
      "elapsedTime": "time"
    },
    "timeSeries": {
      "variable": "run log",
      "columns": ["time", "speed"]
    },
    "run": { "mode": "greenFlag" },
    "done": { "mode": "poll", "variable": "time", "timeoutMs": 120000 }
  },
  "pages": [
    {
      "id": "orientation",
      "phase": "Orientation & Conceptualization",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "orientation-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "orientation-media",
              "type": "media",
              "items": [
                { "url": "REPLACE_ME/ball-drop-1.gif", "kind": "gif", "alt": "A large ball is dropped from high up and falls to the ground." },
                { "url": "REPLACE_ME/ball-drop-2.gif", "kind": "gif", "alt": "A smaller ball is dropped and falls to the ground." },
                { "url": "REPLACE_ME/ball-drop-3.gif", "kind": "gif", "alt": "A small ball is dropped from lower down and falls to the ground." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "orientation-prompt",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "Observe the animations above. In the animations, a ball is dropped. What do you observe about the speed of the ball as it falls? What is causing the differences? (For this activity, ignore the moment the ball hits the ground.)"
            },
            {
              "id": "orientation-observe",
              "type": "freeText",
              "key": "observation",
              "placeholder": "I observe... I think this is happening because..."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hypothesis",
      "phase": "Investigation",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "hypothesis-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "hypothesis-intro",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "Let's design experiments examining a ball falling towards the ground. This time, you'll design two experiments!\n\nFill in the blanks and tables below:"
            },
            {
              "id": "hypothesis-set",
              "type": "hypotheses",
              "key": "hypotheses",
              "statement": true,
              "minHypotheses": 2,
              "maxHypotheses": 3,
              "ivOptions": [
                { "id": "variableA", "label": "Variable A" },
                { "id": "variableB", "label": "Variable B" },
                { "id": "variableC", "label": "Variable C" }
              ],
              "dvOptions": [
                { "id": "variableD", "label": "Variable D" },
                { "id": "variableE", "label": "Variable E" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "design",
      "phase": "Investigation",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "design-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "design-intro",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "Let's design experiments examining a ball falling towards the ground.\n\nFill in the table below for each of your hypotheses:"
            },
            {
              "id": "design-trials",
              "type": "trialTable",
              "key": "experimentDesign",
              "hypothesesFrom": "hypotheses",
              "title": "Experiment:",
              "comparePrompt": "We compare the resulting values of:",
              "minTrials": 2,
              "maxTrials": 5
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "run",
      "phase": "Investigation",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "run-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "run-intro",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "Let's run your experiment with the simulation below! You can return to the previous step as needed to review your experiment design.\n\nThe data from each trial will be recorded. You can access them by clicking on the Results button. (Your experiment results from the previous activities can also be accessed.)"
            },
            {
              "id": "run-simulation",
              "type": "simulation",
              "key": "dropRuns",
              "inputs": ["ballMass", "dropHeight"],
              "outputs": ["speed", "kineticEnergy", "potentialEnergy", "elapsedTime"],
              "graph": { "x": "time", "y": ["speed"] },
              "includeTrialsFrom": ["cartPush", "cartFriction"],
              "minRuns": 2
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "conclusion",
      "phase": "Conclusion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "conclusion-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "conclusion-intro",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "Let's reflect on the results. You can go back to the simulation as needed by clicking on the Back button."
            },
            { "id": "conclusion-why", "type": "freeText", "key": "whyResults", "hypothesesFrom": "hypotheses", "prompt": "Why did the results happen? What theory or concept explains this phenomenon?" },
            {
              "id": "conclusion-data",
              "type": "freeText",
              "key": "resultsData",
              "hypothesesFrom": "hypotheses",
              "prompt": "What was the result of your experiment? Explain the data from your results. Does the data support your hypothesis? Why?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "discussion",
      "phase": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "discussion-s1",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "discussion-intro",
              "type": "text",
              "md": "To conclude, write a statement with a claim, evidence, and reasoning.\n\n- The **claim** should be about the collision of the ball and the ground: what was your hypothesis?\n- The **evidence** should include your experiment results. Be specific about the experiments you ran!\n- The **reasoning** should mention the physics concepts that explain your results."
            },
            { "id": "discussion-cer", "type": "freeText", "key": "cer", "hypothesesFrom": "hypotheses", "placeholder": "Enter here...", "rows": 8 }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "formative",
      "phase": "Formative Assessment",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "formative-s1",
          "blocks": [
            { "id": "formative-intro", "type": "text", "md": "Let's end with a quick test of your understanding." },
            {
              "id": "formative-half-height",
              "type": "freeText",
              "key": "halfHeight",
              "prompt": "Suppose a ball is being dropped to the ground. If we halved the drop height of the ball, how would the ball's movement be affected? Point out the variables that would be affected or unaffected, and explain how and why that would be the case.",
              "placeholder": "Enter here...",
              "rows": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
